From e1b5d21b09bb8db27c36f8db1f9f3d9b865a1525 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): translate command block edits to Bedrock

Java 26.3 edits command blocks through a dedicated serverbound packet, which ViaBedrock did not handle. Translate its mode and flags to the Bedrock 2193 update packet so closing the editor applies the change. Preserve Bedrock-only block entity settings that the Java editor cannot display.

Preserve TickDelay and ExecuteOnFirstTick in a bounded native edit payload. A native COMMAND_BLOCK container now opens the Java editor from its authoritative loaded tag, with operator permission checks and a matching native window close lifecycle. Java lacks these native fields, so an advertised addon channel carries complete edits. Codec, session and command-mode tests cover invalid fields and close gating.
